<title>NEPAL: Japanese monk killed at Lord Buddha's birthplace.</title>
<headline>Japanese monk killed at Lord Buddha's birthplace.</headline>
<dateline>KATHMANDU 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Japanese monk was shot dead by unidentified gunmen in a Nepali town that Buddhists believe was the birthplace of the Lord Buddha, state radio said on Friday.</p>
<p>Radio Nepal said Yonataka Nawatami was shot on Thursday at Lumbini, 350 km (220 miles) west of Kathmandu.</p>
<p>One person was injured and six were taken into custody, it said giving no other details.</p>
</text>
